From 16d3b6848302add7c3868b4436ad75dd92ff6217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Super User <root@localhost.localdomain>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 00:38:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] KVM: arm64: Disable HDBSS when dirty ring mode is
 enabled

HDBSS currently only supports dirty bitmap mode, not dirty ring mode.
Since the two mechanisms are incompatible (HDBSS flushes to bitmap while
QEMU reads from ring), disable HDBSS when dirty ring is enabled.

This is a temporary workaround until HDBSS dirty ring support is implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c
index 22d2cf60c965..797a2df048b7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c
@@ -26,6 +26,10 @@ int kvm_arm_enable_hdbss_internal(struct kvm *kvm, u64 order)
 	if (!system_supports_hdbss())
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* HDBSS doesn't support dirty ring mode yet */
+	if (kvm->dirty_ring_size)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	if (order > HDBSS_MAX_SIZE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
